     "page": 1,
     "text": "Cowan Harris and Medina Medical Group\nRe: Sandra Fisher (DOB 07/23/1977)\n\nApril 10, 2026: Sandra Fisher, a 48-year-old female, presented today for her annual physical examination. During this visit, her blood pressure was recorded at 115/82 and her weight was 224 pounds. Ms. Fisher has a known history of Type 1 diabetes, which was diagnosed at the age 40. Currently, her diabetes well-controlled, with her most recent A1c reading at 7.2. She has been on insulin therapy for the past 8.3 years and continues to take insulin glargine 100 u/mL and insulin lispro 100 u/mL. She is compliant with her insulin regimen and has no complications such as microalbuminuria, neuropathy, retinopathy, or coronary artery disease. \n\nOctober 10, 2024: Sandra Fisher visited the clinic for a follow-up regarding her Type 1 diabetes. At that time, her blood pressure was noted at 120/87 and her weight was pounds. Ms. Fisher is doing well, managing her diabetes effectively. She continues to maintain her insulin therapy with insulin glargine 100 u/mL and insulin lispro 100 u/mL. The A1c reading taken during this visit was 7.5. \n\nApril 12, 2023: Ms. Fisher came in for a routine check-up concerning her Type 1 diabetes. Her blood pressure at this visit was 122/79 and her weight was 219 pounds. She was doing well at the time, and her diabetes was being well She continues her insulin therapy with insulin glargine 100 u/mL and insulin lispro 100 u/mL. The A1c reading taken during this visit was also 7.5.\n\nA1C trend: The A1c readings over the past few years have been as follows: 7.2 on April 26, on October 24, and 7.5 on April 23. \n\nExercise: Ms. Fisher has been quite active, engaging in running three to four times a week, which has been beneficial for her overall health and diabetes management.\n\nSocial: Regarding her lifestyle, Ms. Fisher consumes alcohol approximately two times a week, which amounts to around two drinks.\n\n[attached outside lab - Heritage Diagnostic Services 09-04-11]\nCHOL / HDL 301 / 69\nFRUCTOSAMINE 251\nNICOTINE METAB NEG\nGAMMA GT 36\n\nThe lab from Heritage Diagnostic Services, dated September 2011, show a cholesterol level of 301 with an HDL of 69. The fructosamine level was 251. The nicotine metabolite test was negative, and the gamma-glutamyl transferase (GGT) level was 36.\n\nThis summary provides a comprehensive overview of Ms. Fisher's health status, diabetes management, and associated laboratory findings. Please let me know if need any further information. \n\nSincerely,\n\nDr. Amy Johnson, MD\nEndocrinology\nCowan Harris and Medina"
